Nice catch, and thanks for pasting the error – that helps a lot.

Two things going on:

1. **The Substring error** in `CopyDGFSToUSB.ps1` is because for at least one file, `$file.FullName` isn’t as long as `$sourceRoot.Length`, so `Substring()` blows up.
2. The `Macrium ÔåÆ USB` text is just mojibake from the Unicode arrow I originally used. We’ll clean that too.

Let’s fix the important one first.

---

## ✅ Fixed `CopyDGFSToUSB.ps1` (no Substring errors, robust relative paths)

Replace the entire contents of **`D:\Backup\CopyDGFSToUSB.ps1`** with this:

```powershell
# CopyDGFSToUSB.ps1
# Mirror NAS D-GFS folder to USB D-GFS folder (by filename/relative path)

$Source      = "\\inv-nas-01\Share-INV-LAP-01\MacriumReflect\D-GFS"
$Destination = "F:\MacriumReflect\D-GFS"
$LogFile     = "D:\Backup\CopyDGFSToUSB.log"

# Ensure destination root exists
if (!(Test-Path $Destination)) {
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $Destination -Force | Out-Null
}

# Collect NAS files
$nasFiles = @()
if (Test-Path $Source) {
    $nasFiles = Get-ChildItem $Source -Recurse -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
}

# Build map of NAS relative paths
$nasRelPaths = @{}

foreach ($file in $nasFiles) {
    $full = $file.FullName

    # Only process if the full path starts with $Source
    if ($full.StartsWith($Source, [System.StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) {
        $rel = $full.Substring($Source.Length).TrimStart('\', '/')
        if ($rel) {
            $nasRelPaths[$rel] = $true
        }
    }
}

# Remove files on USB that are not on NAS (by relative path)
if (Test-Path $Destination) {
    $usbFiles = Get-ChildItem $Destination -Recurse -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

    foreach ($file in $usbFiles) {
        $full = $file.FullName
        $rel = $null

        if ($full.StartsWith($Destination, [System.StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) {
            $rel = $full.Substring($Destination.Length).TrimStart('\', '/')
        }

        if ($rel -and -not $nasRelPaths.ContainsKey($rel)) {
            Remove-Item $file.FullName -Force
        }
    }
}

# Build map of USB relative paths (after cleanup)
$usbRelPaths = @{}
if (Test-Path $Destination) {
    $usbFiles = Get-ChildItem $Destination -Recurse -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

    foreach ($file in $usbFiles) {
        $full = $file.FullName
        if ($full.StartsWith($Destination, [System.StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) {
            $rel = $full.Substring($Destination.Length).TrimStart('\', '/')
            if ($rel) {
                $usbRelPaths[$rel] = $true
            }
        }
    }
}

# Copy missing files from NAS to USB
foreach ($file in $nasFiles) {
    $full = $file.FullName

    if ($full.StartsWith($Source, [System.StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) {
        $rel = $full.Substring($Source.Length).TrimStart('\', '/')
        if (-not $rel) { continue }

        if (-not $usbRelPaths.ContainsKey($rel)) {
            $destPath = Join-Path $Destination $rel
            $destDir  = Split-Path $destPath

            if (!(Test-Path $destDir)) {
                New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $destDir -Force | Out-Null
            }

            Copy-Item $full -Destination $destPath -Force
        }
    }
}

# Log
$Timestamp = (Get-Date).ToString("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss")
"$Timestamp - Synced D-GFS folder (NAS -> USB by relative path)" | Out-File -FilePath $LogFile -Append -Encoding ASCII
```

Key changes:

- Dropped the `Resolve-Path` / `$sourceRoot` complexity.
- Only call `Substring()` **after** checking `StartsWith($Source)`.
- Always `TrimStart('\', '/')` after the Substring to get a clean relative path.
- Everything is ASCII-safe.

This should get rid of the `startIndex cannot be larger than length of string` errors.

---

## ✅ Clean up `RunToUSB.cmd` text (ASCII only)

The mojibake `Macrium ÔåÆ USB Sync Jobs` is just the Unicode arrow being mis-decoded. Let’s make sure your `.cmd` is pure ASCII.

Update **`D:\Backup\RunToUSB.cmd`** to this:

```cmd
@echo off
setlocal

set "SCRIPT_DIR=%~dp0"

echo ============================================
echo Running Macrium to USB Sync Jobs
echo ============================================
echo.

echo [1/2] Syncing Laptop Images...
powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "%SCRIPT_DIR%CopyImagesToUSB.ps1"
echo.

echo [2/2] Syncing D-GFS Backup...
powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "%SCRIPT_DIR%CopyDGFSToUSB.ps1"
echo.

echo ============================================
echo All sync tasks completed.
echo ============================================

endlocal
```

No fancy characters, just plain ASCII.

---

## Next step

1. Overwrite `CopyDGFSToUSB.ps1` with the new version above.  
2. Overwrite `RunToUSB.cmd` with the ASCII version.  
3. Run from a PowerShell prompt:

   ```powershell
   D:\Backup\RunToUSB.cmd
   ```

You should see both steps run without errors, and your logs updating.

